## §3 Account and Registration

### §3.1 Account Creation

The App can generally be used without an account. An account is required if you wish to use:

- Push notifications
- Cloud-based streak tracking
- Future synchronization features (planned)

Registration requires a valid email address and a secure password.

### §3.2 User Obligations

You agree to:

- Provide truthful information during registration
- Keep your login credentials confidential and not share them with third parties
- Inform us immediately if you suspect misuse of your account
- Not misuse the App or use it for unlawful purposes

### §3.3 Account Security

We implement technical and organizational measures to protect your account:

- **Password Hashing:** Your password is hashed using an iterative SHA-256 process (10,000 rounds) with a random salt before being transmitted to Firebase
- **Device Fingerprinting:** The App creates a SHA-256 hash from device information to detect suspicious login attempts
- **Security Log:** The App logs security events (login attempts, account changes) locally on your device

You are responsible for choosing a strong password and keeping your credentials secure.

### §3.4 Account Deletion

You may permanently delete your account at any time in the App settings under "Delete Account."

**Consequences of account deletion:**
- All account data in Firebase (email, display name, push tokens, activity data) is permanently deleted
- All local data (decisions, boards, journal entries with photos and voice notes) is removed from your device
- **Security log:** Locally stored security events are not completely deleted but anonymized. The email address in events is replaced with "[deleted]," while device information and timestamps are retained for security reasons (fraud prevention, traceability of security incidents)

**Deleted data cannot be restored.**

---

## §4 Data Protection and Data Processing

### §4.1 Applicability of the Privacy Policy

Our separate Privacy Policy applies to the processing of personal data and forms an integral part of these Terms of Use.

### §4.2 Local Data Storage

All your decision-related content is stored exclusively locally on your device:

- Boards and cards with all ratings
- Journal entries with text, photos (up to 5 per entry), and voice notes
- Comments and checklists on cards
- Onboarding survey data (decision context, preferred style, desired outcomes)
- Local profiling results (archetypes, pattern analysis)

**This data never leaves your device** and is not transmitted to us or third parties.

### §4.3 Cloud Storage

To provide certain features, we store the following data in the cloud (Firebase / Google LLC, USA):

- **Account Data:** Email address, password (encrypted), display name, user ID
- **Push Notification Data:** Expo push token, platform (iOS/Android), app version
- **Activity Data for Notification Logic:** Timestamp of last decision, streak count

**Decision content (boards, cards, journal texts, photos, voice notes) is NOT stored in the cloud.**

### §4.4 Android Backup

The App allows Android system backups. This means that your locally stored App data may be included in Android cloud backups (Google Drive) if this feature is enabled on your device. You can disable Android backups for Vayze in Android settings under "Google > Backup."

