## §9 Third-Party Services

### §9.1 Services Used

We use the following third-party services:

| Service | Provider | Purpose |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Firebase Authentication | Google LLC, USA | Account management, login, password reset |
| Firebase Firestore | Google LLC, USA | Storage of push tokens, activity data |
| Firebase Cloud Functions | Google LLC, USA | Serverless logic for push notifications |
| Expo Push Notification Service | Expo Inc., USA | Technical delivery of push notifications |
| Firebase Analytics (optional, currently inactive) | Google LLC, USA | Usage statistics (opt-in only) |

**Third-party privacy policies:**
- Google Firebase: https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy
- Expo: https://expo.dev/privacy

### §9.2 Data Transfer to the USA

All cloud services used are operated by providers based in the USA. Data transfers are carried out on the basis of EU Standard Contractual Clauses pursuant to Art. 46(2)(c) GDPR.

**Note:** The USA currently does not have an adequacy decision by the EU Commission. There is a risk that US authorities may access your data under certain circumstances.

### §9.3 No Control Over Third Parties

We have no control over third-party data processing practices. The respective providers are responsible for their data protection practices.

### §9.4 Account Deletion at Third Parties

When deleting your Vayze account, your data will also be deleted from our processors (Firebase). Security logs stored locally on your device are anonymized but not fully deleted (see §3.4).

