## §10 Analytics and Tracking

### §10.1 Analytics Function

The App includes an analytics infrastructure (Firebase Analytics), which is **currently de facto inactive** because the required module is not enabled in the App configuration.

**Status:** The analytics setting in the App is present but currently has no function.

**If the analytics function is activated in future versions**, the following event data would be transmitted to Google Firebase Analytics (USA) when the analytics setting is enabled:
- Decision events (start, completion) with mode, category, and weighting preset
- Journal events (creation, deletion) with metadata (word count, whether photos/audio are present)
- Navigation events (tab changes)

**No content is ever transmitted to Analytics.**

### §10.2 Opt-Out

You can disable the analytics function at any time in the App settings. By default, analytics is disabled.

### §10.3 No Tracking Outside the App

We do not use tracking pixels, cookies, or similar technologies to track your behavior outside the App.

